{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The user hits send while the reply is in flight. You need a rule for that message: wait, ignore, or cut in."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default the message waits in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":". It sends after the current run succeeds."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-show-the-pending-queue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Show the pending queue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" separately from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelQueued(id)"},{"type":"text","value":" drops an item before it sends:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages, queue, sendMessage, cancelQueued } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=queueing-messages"},{"type":"code","value":"function PendingQueue() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      {queue.map((item) => (\n        <div key={item.id} className=\"pending\">\n          {typeof item.content === \"string\" ? item.content : \"[attachment]\"}\n          <button onClick={() => cancelQueued(item.id)}>Cancel</button>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=queueing-messages"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" with a different style from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":". Once the text appears in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", clear the composer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-pick-whenbusy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Pick "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenBusy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" option. A string is shorthand for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ whenBusy }"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  queue: { whenBusy: \"queue\", drain: \"fifo\", maxSize: 5 },\n});","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=queueing-whenbusy"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenBusy"},{"type":"text","value":" is what happens to a send that arrives while the client is busy. The client is busy when a stream is active, a send is in flight, or the queue is draining:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"queue\""},{"type":"text","value":" (default): hold the message. It sends once the run settles successfully."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"drop\""},{"type":"text","value":": ignore the send. The promise still resolves. The message never appears in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep the composer text and show feedback if you want a retry."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"interrupt\""},{"type":"text","value":": abort the current stream and send the new message now. Already-queued messages stay. They drain after the interrupting send succeeds."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override the policy for one send with the second argument to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"sendMessage(\"Never mind, do this instead\", {\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n  body: { source: \"composer\" },\n});","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=queueing-whenbusy"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" is extra JSON for that request only. It is merged into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"later","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Later"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"drain"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"fifo\""},{"type":"text","value":" (default) sends queued items one at a time in order. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"batch\""},{"type":"text","value":" merges the queue into one send after a successful settle (strings join with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\\n"},{"type":"text","value":", multimodal parts stay in order, last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" wins)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"}]},{"type":"text","value":": caps how many messages can wait ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" means never queue)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onOverflow"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"reject\""},{"type":"text","value":" (default) ignores a send once "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":" is reached. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"drop-oldest\""},{"type":"text","value":" evicts the oldest queued item to make room."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy function"}]},{"type":"text","value":": pass a function as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" for per-send control. That form always drains FIFO. Per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenBusy"},{"type":"text","value":" still wins."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"when-the-queue-drains-versus-flushes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the queue drains versus flushes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drain (auto-send)"}]},{"type":"text","value":": only after a successful stream settle, including after tool continuations finish."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flush (discard without sending)"}]},{"type":"text","value":": on error or abort of the active generation ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":", real stream errors), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unsubscribe()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reload()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" does not flush"}]},{"type":"text","value":": existing queued items remain. They drain after the interrupting turn succeeds."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The composer no longer fights the stream. A send while busy waits, drops, or cuts in, on purpose."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-show-the-pending-queue","text":"1. Show the pending queue","level":2},{"id":"2-pick-whenbusy","text":"2. Pick whenBusy","level":2},{"id":"later","text":"Later","level":2},{"id":"when-the-queue-drains-versus-flushes","text":"When the queue drains versus flushes","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe user hits send while the reply is in flight. You need a rule for that message: wait, ignore, or cut in.\n\nBy default the message waits in `queue`. It sends after the current run succeeds.\n\n## 1. Show the pending queue\n\n`useChat` exposes `queue` separately from `messages`. `cancelQueued(id)` drops an item before it sends:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-messages\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages, queue, sendMessage, cancelQueued } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n```\n\n```tsx group=queueing-messages\nfunction PendingQueue() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      {queue.map((item) => (\n        <div key={item.id} className=\"pending\">\n          {typeof item.content === \"string\" ? item.content : \"[attachment]\"}\n          <button onClick={() => cancelQueued(item.id)}>Cancel</button>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nRender `queue` with a different style from `messages`. Once the text appears in `queue` or `messages`, clear the composer.\n\n## 2. Pick `whenBusy`\n\nPass a `queue` option. A string is shorthand for `{ whenBusy }`:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-whenbusy\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  queue: { whenBusy: \"queue\", drain: \"fifo\", maxSize: 5 },\n});\n```\n\n`whenBusy` is what happens to a send that arrives while the client is busy. The client is busy when a stream is active, a send is in flight, or the queue is draining:\n\n- `\"queue\"` (default): hold the message. It sends once the run settles successfully.\n- `\"drop\"`: ignore the send. The promise still resolves. The message never appears in `queue` or `messages`. Keep the composer text and show feedback if you want a retry.\n- `\"interrupt\"`: abort the current stream and send the new message now. Already-queued messages stay. They drain after the interrupting send succeeds.\n\nOverride the policy for one send with the second argument to `sendMessage`:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-whenbusy\nsendMessage(\"Never mind, do this instead\", {\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n  body: { source: \"composer\" },\n});\n```\n\n`body` is extra JSON for that request only. It is merged into `forwardedProps`.\n\n## Later\n\n- **`drain`**: `\"fifo\"` (default) sends queued items one at a time in order. `\"batch\"` merges the queue into one send after a successful settle (strings join with `\\n`, multimodal parts stay in order, last `body` wins).\n- **`maxSize`**: caps how many messages can wait (`0` means never queue).\n- **`onOverflow`**: `\"reject\"` (default) ignores a send once `maxSize` is reached. `\"drop-oldest\"` evicts the oldest queued item to make room.\n- **Strategy function**: pass a function as `queue` for per-send control. That form always drains FIFO. Per-call `whenBusy` still wins.\n\n### When the queue drains versus flushes\n\n- **Drain (auto-send)**: only after a successful stream settle, including after tool continuations finish.\n- **Flush (discard without sending)**: on error or abort of the active generation (`stop()`, real stream errors), `clear()`, `unsubscribe()`, and `reload()`.\n- **`interrupt` does not flush**: existing queued items remain. They drain after the interrupting turn succeeds.\n\nThe composer no longer fights the stream. A send while busy waits, drops, or cuts in, on purpose.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Message Queue\nid: message-queue\norder: 4\ndescription: \"Control what happens when the user sends while a reply is still streaming: queue, drop, or interrupt.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - message queue\n  - queue\n  - whenBusy\n  - interrupt\n  - sendMessage\n  - cancelQueued\n---\n\nThe user hits send while the reply is in flight. You need a rule for that message: wait, ignore, or cut in.\n\nBy default the message waits in `queue`. It sends after the current run succeeds.\n\n## 1. Show the pending queue\n\n`useChat` exposes `queue` separately from `messages`. `cancelQueued(id)` drops an item before it sends:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-messages\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages, queue, sendMessage, cancelQueued } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n```\n\n```tsx group=queueing-messages\nfunction PendingQueue() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      {queue.map((item) => (\n        <div key={item.id} className=\"pending\">\n          {typeof item.content === \"string\" ? item.content : \"[attachment]\"}\n          <button onClick={() => cancelQueued(item.id)}>Cancel</button>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nRender `queue` with a different style from `messages`. Once the text appears in `queue` or `messages`, clear the composer.\n\n## 2. Pick `whenBusy`\n\nPass a `queue` option. A string is shorthand for `{ whenBusy }`:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-whenbusy\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { sendMessage } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  queue: { whenBusy: \"queue\", drain: \"fifo\", maxSize: 5 },\n});\n```\n\n`whenBusy` is what happens to a send that arrives while the client is busy. The client is busy when a stream is active, a send is in flight, or the queue is draining:\n\n- `\"queue\"` (default): hold the message. It sends once the run settles successfully.\n- `\"drop\"`: ignore the send. The promise still resolves. The message never appears in `queue` or `messages`. Keep the composer text and show feedback if you want a retry.\n- `\"interrupt\"`: abort the current stream and send the new message now. Already-queued messages stay. They drain after the interrupting send succeeds.\n\nOverride the policy for one send with the second argument to `sendMessage`:\n\n```tsx group=queueing-whenbusy\nsendMessage(\"Never mind, do this instead\", {\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n  body: { source: \"composer\" },\n});\n```\n\n`body` is extra JSON for that request only. It is merged into `forwardedProps`.\n\n## Later\n\n- **`drain`**: `\"fifo\"` (default) sends queued items one at a time in order. `\"batch\"` merges the queue into one send after a successful settle (strings join with `\\n`, multimodal parts stay in order, last `body` wins).\n- **`maxSize`**: caps how many messages can wait (`0` means never queue).\n- **`onOverflow`**: `\"reject\"` (default) ignores a send once `maxSize` is reached. `\"drop-oldest\"` evicts the oldest queued item to make room.\n- **Strategy function**: pass a function as `queue` for per-send control. That form always drains FIFO. Per-call `whenBusy` still wins.\n\n### When the queue drains versus flushes\n\n- **Drain (auto-send)**: only after a successful stream settle, including after tool continuations finish.\n- **Flush (discard without sending)**: on error or abort of the active generation (`stop()`, real stream errors), `clear()`, `unsubscribe()`, and `reload()`.\n- **`interrupt` does not flush**: existing queued items remain. They drain after the interrupting turn succeeds.\n\nThe composer no longer fights the stream. A send while busy waits, drops, or cuts in, on purpose.\n"}
